# Findings gitleaks has already adjudicated, one fingerprint per line
# (`<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>`). Fingerprints are pinned to a specific
# commit, so an entry here suppresses exactly one historical finding and can
# never blind the scanner on a future diff — unlike a path or regex
# allowlist in `.gitleaks.toml`.
#
# #617 / PR #631. The e2e added in 6f6b4cd passes a stand-in credential to
# the auth pre-flight and writes another into a fixture `.npmrc`; the local
# stand-in registry the test spawns never reads either. Both were
# `piot-e2e-*-placeholder` strings, whose Shannon entropy (3.77 / 3.52)
# clears generic-api-key's 3.5 threshold when they sit next to the word
# "token". d1e1eff replaced them with a low-entropy `not-a-token`, but
# gitleaks scans every commit in a PR, not just its head, so the original
# commit still trips it.
#
# These two entries die with the squash-merge that collapses this branch —
# the commit they name will not exist on main.
